//
// TWO WIDENINGS AT ONE POSITION ARE REFUSED (`@FR-Disp-Ambiguous`, ranked by
// `@FR-Disp-Specific`): a `u8` widens into `integer` and into `i16` alike (C-Int — both ranges
// hold 0..=255), so the two members rank WIDENED at the only position and neither is more
// specific.  The rank table does not order two ranges that both hold the argument by their
// size, so the call is refused naming both, never resolved to the tighter range.  One refusal
// per file.
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; the refusal fired as expected on 18594597b,
//   interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile (the expected diagnostic).
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names both members.
// HOLDS: an `integer` argument is EXACT for `aw(integer)` and is not refused (Disp-Specific's
//   cell).
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `aw(u8)` is ambiguous — it is taken by aw(integer) and aw(i16)

fn aw(x: integer) -> text { "integer {x}" }
fn aw(x: i16) -> text { "i16 {x}" }

fn main() {
  b: u8 = 7;
  println(aw(b));
}
